1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,504
My shadow stopped following me three days ago. Now I walk through the world like a ghost in daylight.

2
00:00:06,804 --> 00:00:15,420
I checked the pavement everywhere, but the light hit the concrete and found nothing. Just empty, gray, lonely space.

3
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:23,232
The doctors say I’m perfectly healthy. They look at my vitals, but they never seem to look at the ground.

4
00:00:23,532 --> 00:00:29,820
Then, in the subway station, I saw it. A shadow attached to my feet, but it wasn't mine at all.

5
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:38,184
It was smaller, jagged, and it moved faster than my own body. It was dancing to a song I couldn't hear.

6
00:00:38,484 --> 00:00:46,020
I chased the shadow into the darkest alley. I needed to know why it was haunting my heavy, empty steps.

7
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:53,832
I pulled my phone out and used the flash. The light hit the wall and the shadow stood up, revealed.

8
00:00:54,132 --> 00:01:02,148
It wasn't a shadow. It was a projection. A girl, glowing with blue light, reaching back through a shimmering rift.

9
00:01:02,448 --> 00:01:09,000
She whispered that she was my daughter, calling me back from a future where I never actually got to be born.

10
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:15,132
I realized then that I am not the man. I am just the memory she is trying to keep alive.
